 "hypothesis": "H36-1 (SPI-GM Subsurface Blind-Fault Expert + Elkan Prior-Shift Calibration + Exact 300 m Submodular Marginal-Credit Cover): correcting the 200x potential-field gradient unit mismatch in Family A via local magnetic/gravity source wavenumber (H36_mag_spi_k, H36_grav_spi_k), training a zero-topography subsurface fault expert (C + E + H36, 0 DEM / 0 LiDAR features) plus a cover-adaptive Product-of-Experts fusion with BDE+7, calibrating posterior probabilities under Elkan (2001) prior-shift, and replacing greedy 2.4-px spacing with exact Minoux lazy-greedy maximization of the asymmetric Tversky numerator on the 300 m kernel (d(catalogue) > 200 m) improves blind/covered fault recovery and yields a genuinely unique non-topographic GeoTIFF.",
 "mechanism": "Hydrothermal upflow along buried Basin-and-Range step-overs, accommodation zones, and pediment-covered range fronts destroys titanomagnetite or juxtaposes basement blocks across steeply dipping contacts (sharp unit-corrected H36_mag_spi_k & omnidirectional H36_grav_spi_k wavenumbers + 150 m upward-continuation persistence H36_up150_persist + strike concordance H36_gm_strike_concord), creates conductive clay/brine smearing at 2 km MT depth + shallow conductive-base cupolas + heat-flow disequilibrium (H36_chem_diseq, H36_transtension_iq), and concentrates microseismicity near brittle fault tips even where Holocene alluvial/playa sedimentation erases surface scarps (H36_burial_regime). Exact 300 m submodular selection allocates 37,654 off-catalogue (d > 200 m) binary dots by true expected 29-pixel kernel marginal credit.",
 "non_fault_process_that_could_mimic_it": "Unfaulted Tertiary ash-flow tuff / basalt paleochannel pinch-outs and pluton-country-rock intrusive contacts (strong SPI_mag and gravity wavenumber ridges without brittle permeability), closed-basin evaporite/playa clay lenses producing shallow conductive MT anomalies without fault-controlled upflow, and mining/geothermal injection seismicity clusters.",
